	"reviewNotes": [
		"The Bassa-Nge speak Nupe Tako but are mapped as their own people later; the Kakanda and Kupa are related but separate.",
		"Nupe in the FCT and in Kwara beyond Edu and Pategi (for example Lafiagi’s surroundings, Moro) are not yet mapped.",
		"Nupe communities outside Niger and Kwara follow Sidi (2023), who lists Lokoja, Ajaokuta, Shintaku, Koton Karfe, Abaji, Eggan, Budam, Umaisha, Toto, Shamenge, Gadabuke, Gwagwalada and Zuba as Nupe-speaking. Budam, Shamenge and Gadabuke are not located in GRID3.",
		"Nupe communities outside Niger and Kwara follow Sidi (2023), who lists Lokoja, Ajaokuta, Shintaku, Koton Karfe, Abaji, Eggan, Budam, Umaisha, Toto, Shamenge, Gadabuke, Gwagwalada and Zuba as Nupe-speaking. Budam, Shamenge and Gadabuke are not located in GRID3."
	]
